  "description": "Anatomy of the qou_mass binding over-prediction. The error is NON-MONOTONIC in A (peak +36.5% at 6Li, minimum ~+5% at 12C-16O, then rising again to +19.5% at 40Ca), which rules out a single mis-scaled coefficient. TWO independent components. (1) A=5..11: the model has NO p-shell dip -- experiment falls 1.74 MeV/A from 4He to 6Li, the model falls 0.21, and experimental B/A has 5.9x the variance of the model's over A=4..16. The +36% spike is the ABSENCE of the experimental dip, not an A-dependence error. (2) A>=12: the model's B/A is LINEAR in A (fit 7.0862 + 0.0781674*A, max residual 0.33 MeV/A over A=4..40), so B is QUADRATIC in A -- complete-graph C(A,2) pair counting with epsilon = 0.156335 MeV per pair-bond. That is exactly the z = A-1 law that QOU.Mass.CoordinationSaturation refutes structurally: complete graph gives unbounded B/A, bounded degree gives constant, and observed saturation forces bounded degree. The Lean proves what the model must satisfy; the live compute does not satisfy it. Does NOT localise the A^2 term in source, and does NOT claim fixing one component fixes the other -- they are independent.",
